      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The Cove revolutionized activist documentary filmmaking through its thrilling blend of covert operations and environmental exposé. Using hidden cameras and military-grade thermal technology, director Louie Psihoyos and activist Ric O'Barry infiltrated Taiji, Japan to document the secretive dolphin hunting industry. The film shares DNA with earlier eco-docs like <a href=\"/movie/1781\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1781\">An Inconvenient Truth</a> (2006) but elevates the format by structuring itself as a heart-pounding heist movie. This approach influenced later activist docs like <a href=\"/movie/158999\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"158999\">Blackfish</a> (2013) and The Ghost Fleet (2018)."
      },
