      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film sparked a wave of ocean conservation documentaries that combine stunning underwater photography with urgent environmental messaging. <a href=\"/movie/286407\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"286407\">Mission Blue</a> (2014) profiles oceanographer Sylvia Earle's campaign to establish marine protected areas. <a href=\"/movie/432615\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"432615\">Chasing Coral</a> (2017) uses time-lapse cameras to capture coral reef bleaching, while <a href=\"/movie/431339\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"431339\">A Plastic Ocean</a> (2016) reveals the devastating impact of plastic pollution through immersive cinematography."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The investigative techniques pioneered in The Cove influenced a new generation of whistleblower documentaries. <a href=\"/movie/293310\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"293310\">Citizenfour</a> (2014) used clandestine filming to document Edward Snowden's NSA revelations. <a href=\"/movie/123678\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"123678\">The Act of Killing</a> (2012) employed dramatic reenactments to expose Indonesian genocide perpetrators, while <a href=\"/movie/263614\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"263614\">Virunga</a> (2014) combined undercover footage with conservation advocacy. SUBHEAD: Impact on Environmental Activism"
      },
