      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's success demonstrated documentary's power to drive real-world change. After The Cove's release, several Japanese towns suspended dolphin hunting, while <a href=\"/movie/1781\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1781\">An Inconvenient Truth</a> (2006) helped mainstream climate change discourse. Similarly, <a href=\"/movie/18570\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"18570\">Food, Inc.</a> (2008) transformed public understanding of industrial agriculture, and <a href=\"/movie/40663\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"40663\">Gasland</a> (2010) brought fracking concerns into national debate."
      }
